# Discovery: Gitignore Integration

Spec: GitignoreIntegration

Purpose:
  Define how discovery, analysis, and /sdd case execution honor the
  repository's ignore surfaces (.gitignore, .dockerignore). Ignored
  files are NOT part of the project model: no tasks are generated
  against them, no skill analysis runs over them, no case execution
  modifies them — with explicit, recorded exceptions.

Owns: discovery/gitignore-integration.sdd

Sources:
  Phase 156 (2026-09-14): user directive "after .sdd analysis, case
  execution must account for .gitignore/.dockerignore and similar".

Surfaces:

  gitignore:
    authority: REPO MODEL — authoritative for what belongs to the
      project model. Ignored paths are outside the model.
    examples: tmp/, var/, node_modules/, prompts/inbox/ (runtime
      prompt artifacts), .env* (secrets — never read, never logged).

  dockerignore:
    authority: SANDBOX CONTEXT — advisory for image minimalism and
      secret-free builds ([R59]-[R66]); it constrains WHAT the
      sandbox sees, not what the repo model contains.
    rule: a file can be tracked in git yet excluded from the image
      (docs/, prompts/ are tracked AND dockerignored — correct:
      the sandbox does not need them; the repo does).

Rules:

  [GI1] Case execution MUST NOT modify, generate tasks against, or
        "fix" any gitignored path. Ignored paths are user-owned
        runtime surfaces (tmp/, var/, inbox/).
  [GI2] Discovery reports ignored paths as UNMANAGED SURFACE only
        (existence, size class) — it does not parse their content
        into the project model.
  [GI3] A file that is BOTH tracked and gitignored (drift — e.g.
        prompts/inbox/165-.md while .gitignore declares
        prompts/inbox/) is a DRIFT FINDING: recommend
        `git rm --cached <file>` so tracking matches the declared
        model. Disk copies are preserved.
  [GI4] .gitignore is authoritative for the repo model;
        .dockerignore is advisory for the sandbox image ([R59]
        sandbox minimality). A conflict between them is resolved
        in favor of .gitignore for model questions, .dockerignore
        for image questions.
  [GI5] Exceptions to any [GI] rule require a DEC record
        (reason, owner, scope) — e.g. prompts/history/ is ignored-
        adjacent but deliberately TRACKED because it is the
        append-only prompt-pair ledger ([R104]).
  [GI6] Scanners (mojibake, AZ-language, retired-name) honor the
        ignore surfaces: they scan TRACKED files plus explicitly
        allowed audit surfaces (prompts/history/), never ignored
        runtime directories.

AllowedAuditSurfaces:
  - prompts/history/ (tracked ledger — [R104] append-only audit)
  - .claude/sdd/workflow.yaml + orchestrator.md (stateful flow
    config — deliberately un-ignored in .gitignore)

